   "chapter": "Do you swallow spiders in your sleep?",
   "tier": "MYTH",
   "danger": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "m": "hook",
     "say": "Do you really swallow spiders in your sleep? Eight a year, they say.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     },
     "open": "animal",
     "cast": {
      "creature": "jumping_spider",
      "actor": "jumping_spider",
      "s": 0.75
     },
     "card": {
      "rows": [
       [
        "8 A YEAR?",
        "#ff4b3e",
        130
       ],
       [
        "IN YOUR SLEEP",
        "#ffffff",
        46,
        true
       ]
      ],
      "y": 120,
      "at": "35%"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "escalate",
     "say": "Short answer? No. But the reason why is the best part.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     },
     "cast": {
      "creature": "jumping_spider",
      "actor": "jumping_spider",
      "s": 0.75
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "name",
     "say": "Picture it. Eight spiders a year, crawling into your mouth while you sleep.",
     "card": {
      "rows": [
       [
        "8 SPIDERS A YEAR?",
        "#ffd34d",
        104
       ],
       [
        "IN YOUR SLEEP",
        "#ffffff",
        46,
        true
       ]
      ],
      "y": 150,
      "at": "30%"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "fact",
     "say": "Spider experts say there's no evidence of that. None.",
     "scene": "study",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     },
     "card": {
      "rows": [
       [
        "0",
        "#ffd34d",
        130
       ],
       [
        "EVIDENCE",
        "#ffffff",
        46,
        true
       ]
      ],
      "y": 120,
      "at": "40%"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "fact",
     "say": "And that eight a year number? Nobody has ever found where it really came from.",
     "scene": "study",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "escalate",
     "say": "To a spider, a sleeping human is a giant, breathing, snoring earthquake.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "fact",
     "say": "Your heartbeat and your breathing send out vibrations. To a spider, that's a warning sign.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "fact",
     "say": "Spiders don't go looking for big animals. They go looking for bugs, and quiet corners.",
     "scene": "basement",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "calm",
     "say": "Could one ever wander in? Maybe, once in a lifetime. Eight a year? No.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     }
    },
    {
     "m": "fact",
     "say": "Verdict: myth. You can sleep with your mouth open. Not that you should.",
     "scene": "bedroom",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     },
     "board": {
      "add": true,
      "drop_at": "10%",
      "stamp_at": "26%",
      "off": "60%"
     },
     "gag": false,
     "pad": 0.12
    },
    {
     "m": "escalate",
     "say": "And that's not even the biggest lie about the bugs in your house. Stick around for the roach that lives without its head.",
     "scene": "kitchen",
     "scene_p": {
      "time": "night"
     },
     "cast": {
      "creature": "roach",
      "actor": "cockroach",
      "s": 0.9
     },
     "gag": false
    }
   ]
  },
